WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.711
- [Morgan Freeman] This
story is about a man

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:07.716
with a vision to re-invent
the world's financial system

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:13.096
by creating a truly decentralized
currency for the masses.

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:16.725
That currency was Terra

00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:20.645
and his name was Do Kwon.

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:21.855
- So I said to his face,

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:25.692
"Your size is not size."

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.527
- Right.

00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:29.320
Sorry, the question was,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.031
"State your name and your date of birth,"

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.866
but, uh, moving on, so...

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:33.700
- Sorry to interrupt,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.786
but Francis Coppola said our
self correction mechanisms

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:38.955
won't work when people start panicking.

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:42.167
- Dude, I don't have
time to talk to the poor.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.210
Okay? Especially not on Twitter.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.630
So tell her I ain't got
no time to debate her

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:51.301
and I ain't got no change on
me to give her. (chuckles)

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:52.635
Actually don't tweet that.

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:55.847
That's kind of mean.

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:58.641
- So in the past month I've
been covering stablecoins a lot.

00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:00.977
And my question is,
what makes UST different

00:01:00.977 --> 00:01:02.896
from other stablecoins?

00:01:05.648 --> 00:01:08.568
- UST is not just a stablecoin.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.070
- [Narrator] It was.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.072
- Sure, it's pegged at a dollar.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:12.906
- [Narrator] Not for long.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.116
- But that in itself isn't
what makes stablecoins

00:01:15.116 --> 00:01:17.702
so vital to an ecosystem.

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:18.953
- [Narrator] Here we go again.

00:01:18.953 --> 00:01:21.831
- A decentralized currency is the key

00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:24.042
to building financial infrastructure

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:28.171
that is beyond the reach
of regulations and borders.

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:30.840
And to achieve this,
we need mass adoption,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.302
and to get mass adoption,
we need scalability.

00:01:34.302 --> 00:01:38.556
UST is the only stablecoin
that is yield bearing,

00:01:38.556 --> 00:01:41.476
interchain, and most
importantly, scalable,

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.979
unlike another stablecoin
that I won't name.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:47.315
It's DAI.

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:49.442
You know, DAI from MakerDAO, yeah.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.362
It's the most unscalable
piece of shit I've ever seen.

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:56.074
- And what if UST were

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:57.117
to break the peg?

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.828
Then it would depend on Luna to save UST.

00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:01.329
But the fact that it's depegged,

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:03.581
investors will pull out of
Luna and tank the price.

00:02:03.581 --> 00:02:05.583
So, it's literally a death spiral.

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.919
- (chuckles) Investors pulling out.

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:10.630
Luna is trading at $80 right now.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.716
UST's market cap is at 30 billion,

00:02:13.716 --> 00:02:17.011
making us the third biggest stablecoin.

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:19.264
Does that look like pulling out to you?

00:02:19.264 --> 00:02:23.852
'Cause I know what pulling
out looks like, right?

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:25.270
- [Woman] Yep!

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:28.148
- And that's definitely not it.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:30.108
So if you're trying to spread fud

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:31.484
with your little article,

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.403
then you're gonna have to try
a little harder than that.

00:02:33.403 --> 00:02:34.696
- I'm just trying to get
my questions answered.

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:35.822
- Oh really?

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.906
Are you really?

00:02:36.906 --> 00:02:38.908
Or are you actually from MakerDAO

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:41.327
trying to write a hit piece on Terra?

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.914
Well, here's something
you can write about.

00:02:56.885 --> 00:02:58.428
Ticker, where we at?

00:02:58.428 --> 00:03:00.763
- Luna's at $83, up 4%.

00:03:00.763 --> 00:03:03.224
UST is exactly at a dollar, sir.

00:03:03.224 --> 00:03:04.058
- Beautiful.

00:03:04.058 --> 00:03:06.686
Jimin, how much Bitcoin
do we have in reserve?

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.605
- We bought 1.5 billion worth so far.

00:03:08.605 --> 00:03:10.064
- Make it 10 billion.

00:03:10.064 --> 00:03:12.942
We're gonna be the largest
holder of Bitcoin in the world.

00:03:12.942 --> 00:03:14.903
Jungkook, update.

00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:16.154
- 4pool has been deployed.

00:03:16.154 --> 00:03:17.739
All CVX emissions will go to it.

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:19.908
- You hear that?

00:03:19.908 --> 00:03:22.702
We're going to starve 3pool to death.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.871
It's over for DAI.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.872
- You're crazy.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:28.583
- Why don't you report
back to your little guys

00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:31.252
at Maker DAO that I'm here to stay.

00:03:31.252 --> 00:03:34.422
And not only that, but I'm here to destroy

00:03:34.422 --> 00:03:37.425
every other stablecoin in my way.

00:03:37.425 --> 00:03:40.428
- And by my hand, DAI will die!

00:03:42.096 --> 00:03:43.806
(team cheering)

00:03:43.806 --> 00:03:45.350
- Yeah, let's go.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.560
- This is not sustainable and you know it.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.480
The economics of it makes no sense.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:51.981
- You see my team?

00:03:51.981 --> 00:03:53.524
This is my head of research.

00:03:53.524 --> 00:03:54.484
Look at him!

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:56.277
He has a cryptopunk as his profile,

00:03:56.277 --> 00:03:58.071
so don't talk to me about economics.

00:03:59.197 --> 00:04:00.907
Anyone here dissatisfied

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.784
with how much they've made with Terra?

00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:07.664
Anyone here wanna work
on another blockchain?

00:04:07.664 --> 00:04:08.581
- Fuck no.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.499
- Fuck no.

00:04:11.292 --> 00:04:12.293
- Fuck no.

00:04:12.293 --> 00:04:14.087
- Looks pretty sustainable to me.

00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:16.881
